{"name":"Dromedary","hex":"#e3c295","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dromedary","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in Brighton council area and the Southern Midlands council area, south eastern Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dromedary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dromedary","blocks":[{"text":"The dromedary, also known as the dromedary camel, Arabian camel and one-humped camel, is a large camel of the genus Camelus with one hump on its back. It is the tallest of the three camel species; adult males stand 1.8–2.4 m (5.9–7.9 ft) at the shoulder, while females are 1.7–1.9 m (5.6–6.2 ft) tall. Males typically weigh between 400 and 690 kg, and females weigh between 300 and 540 kg .\nThe dromedary's distinctive features include its long, curved neck, narrow chest, a single hump, and long hairs on the throat, shoulders, and hump. The coat is generally a shade of brown. The hump is 20 cm (7.9 in) tall or more, and is made of fat bound together by fibrous tissue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg/330px-Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dromedary"},{"title":"Dromedary (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Dromedary, also known as the Dromedary Quartet, is an American world music band originally based out of Athens, Georgia, but now with members on both coasts. The group formed as a duo consisting of Andrew Reissiger and Rob McMaken playing a variety of instruments from cultures across the globe. The group's most recent album Sticks and Stones features New Orleans-to-Athens transplant Louis Romanos (percussion) and Chris Enghauser (bass)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dromedary_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg/500px-Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg/1280px-Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg/500px-Camelus_dromedarius_in_Nuweiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamelus_dromedarius_on_Sinai.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg/500px-Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg/1280px-Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg/500px-Dromadaire_d%27Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The dromedary has thick, double-layered eyelashes and bushy eyebrows","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADromadaire_d'Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Dromadaire4478.jpg/500px-Dromadaire4478.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Dromadaire4478.jpg/500px-Dromadaire4478.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The dromedary has a long curved neck, single hump, and long hair on the throat, shoulders, and hump.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADromadaire4478.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Camelus_dromeda